Step 1: Mike made a total of 42 dollars. He spent 10 dollars on new mower blades, so he has the following amount of money left:
42 - 10 = \boxed{32}

Step 2: If Mike wants to buy new 8 dollar games, he needs to find how many of them he can buy with the 32 dollars he has left.
32 / 8 = \boxed{4}

Final Answer: \boxed{4}

Mike can buy 4 eight-dollar games with the money he had left.

